{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "At the Airport"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Check Your Ticket "}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information, involving apologies, thanks, suggestions and invitations in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Letter Y"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">y</span> consonant sound can be difficult to learn. This is because the letter <span class=\"strong\">y</span> can be pronounced as a vowel or a consonant.<br /><br />The letter <span class=\"strong\">y</span> is a consonant when it is the first letter of a syllable that has more than one letter. <br /> <br /> Words like <span class=\"italic\">yes</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">yard</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">you</span> are all examples of  <span class=\"strong\">y</span> as a consonant sound. <br /><br /> Look at the following table to see the difference between <span class=\"strong\">y</span>  as a consonant versus <span class=\"strong\">y</span> as a vowel:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"y\\\" as consonant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"y\\\" as vowel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"crying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"young\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gym\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legroom"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of space you have for your legs in an airplane."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's better food in first class, and more leg room."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in an airport."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "luggage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "suitcase and bags you take on a plane"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You get your luggage first!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to upgrade "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move to a more expensive seat or area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I decided to upgrade my ticket."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anniversary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a celebration of an important event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are having their 50th wedding anniversary party this weekend."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to board"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to enter or go onto a plane or ship"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sounds like we are boarding."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le09ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le09ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Say these words with the Y sound: <span class=\"italic\">yabby</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yacht</span>, yak<span class=\"italic\">yacht</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Yale</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yam</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yank</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yap</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yarn</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yawn</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yay</span>, <span class=\"italic\">year</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yell</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yellow</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yen</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yes</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yet</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yeti</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yoke</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yolk</span>, <span class=\"italic\">you</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yum</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yurt</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say this tongue twister 5 times with a partner. Who can say it the fastest?<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Young Yolanda Yack likes yellow yoyos, yogurt and yummy yams.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, it's your turn to make two tongue twisters! Use words with the letter <span class=\"italic\">Y</span>."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I say and use words with the <span class=\"italic\">y</span> sound."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say tongue twisters with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write tongue twisters with the <span class=\"italic\">y</span> sound."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn3le09ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn3le09ob04re2img02.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn3le09ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: Excuse me. You dropped your ticket. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh thank you very much. You're on flight 981 too?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: Yes, I'm going to visit my parents. They are having their 50th wedding anniversary party this weekend.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: That sounds like fun. Wow ... 50 years ... that's amazing.<br>", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn3le09ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: Your ticket is a different color to mine. Where are you sitting?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: First class. Yesterday, I decided to upgrade my ticket.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: That's nice for you! There's better food, more leg room and ... you get your luggage first!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It was a birthday gift to myself.<br>", "id": 2, "time": "21500", "image": "engenn3le09ob04re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: Well my ticket's not yellow, mine's green ...  back of the plane for me.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I am usually there too! I hope the flight is not delayed or canceled.  The weather outside is terrible.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Female</span>: Sounds like we are boarding. Well, first class passengers anyway. Safe flight!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You too! Enjoy the celebration.<br>", "id": 3, "time": "42000", "image": "engenn3le09ob04re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you like to fly? Do you get nervous?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How often do you fly? Where do you go?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say and use the y sound."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content"